1. The Setup
• Get the Game: Grab it for free from Steam or the official OpenTTD website.
• Start a Map: Click New Game. Keep the climate on Temperate (the green grass option) and set the map size to 512x512. This gives you plenty of room without being overwhelming.
• Get Cash: Unpause the game, click the finance icon (the coin stack), and borrow some money so you have enough capital to build.
2. Your First Route (The Easy Way)
Planes are the easiest way to make money fast because you don't have to lay down tracks or roads.
• Find Two Cities: Look for two large towns that are reasonably far apart.
• Build Airports: Open the airport tool, build a small airport near the center of Town A, and another near the center of Town B.
• Buy a Plane: Click on the hangar at one of the airports, click New Aircraft, buy a passenger plane, and click Orders (the arrow icon).
• Set the Route: Click Go To, click Airport A, click Go To again, and click Airport B.
• Launch: Flip the red "Stopped" button at the bottom of the plane's window to green, and watch the money roll in.
3. Moving to Trains (The Real Game)
Once you have plane money, you can start building railways.
• Find a Match: Look for a Coal Mine and a Power Plant near each other.
• Lay Track: Build a train station right next to the Coal Mine, and another next to the Power Plant. Connect them with a single line of track.
• Add a Depot: Build a train depot connected to your track.
• Buy and Run: Click the depot, buy a locomotive and a few coal hopper cars. Give it orders to Go To the mine station, then Go To the power plant station, and hit start.
